{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,158p;238,307p;331,442p;470,545p;635,715p' src/cljc/yin/shell/cli.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yin.shell.cli\n  \"The command line of the DHT composition\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 6).\n\n   Every `--dht-*` flag, the `keygen` and `dht init|serve|join`\n   subcommands, the publisher's key file, the composition's help text and\n   its startup banner live here and nowhere in the engine tree.  The\n   engine's host driver (`yin.repl.main`) parses the flags it owns, drives\n   one ticker, and takes this namespace's contribution as plain data — a\n   `composition` — so it never names a peer, a principal, a key file or a\n   transport.\n\n   This namespace owns no socket, atom, promise, callback, clock or\n   namespace global either.  Parsing answers data or throws a refusal\n   naming the flag; the key file helpers are the only I/O, and each is an\n   explicit `--dht-key` read or `--dht-keygen` write the operator asked\n   for.\"\n  (:require #?@(:cljd [[\"dart:io\" :as io]]\n                :jolt [[dao.host.text :as text]\n                       [dao.posix.file :as posix-file]])\n            [clojure.string :as str]\n            [dao.space.store.fs :as fs]\n            [dao.stream.datagram :as datagram]\n            [dao.stream.remote-channel :as remote-channel]\n            [yin.repl.main :as repl.main]\n            [yin.repl.state :as state]\n            [yin.shell.dht :as shell.dht]\n            [yin.shell.store :as shell.store]\n            [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]))\n\n\n(defn parse-peer\n  \"A `--dht-peer` value, `host:port` or `[v6-host]:port`, as the DHT's\n   bootstrap contact `{:host h :port p}`.  The host must be an IP\n   literal: the DHT resolves no names.\"\n  [text]\n  (let [[_ v6 v4 port] (re-matches #\"(?:\\[([^\\]]+)\\]|([^:\\[\\]]+)):(\\d+)\"\n                                   (str text))\n        host (or v6 v4)\n        port (repl.main/parse-int port)]\n    (cond\n      (not (datagram/valid-port? port))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-peer takes host:port with a port from 1 \"\n                           \"to 65535, not \" (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      (not (datagram/ip-literal? host))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-peer host must be an IP literal, not \"\n                           (pr-str host))\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      :else {:host host :port port})))\n\n\n(defn- parse-manifest\n  \"A `--dht-manifest` value (the address as printed, with or without its\n   leading colon) as the segment address keyword.\"\n  [text]\n  (when (string? text)\n    (keyword (if (str/starts-with? text \":\") (subs text 1) text))))\n\n\n(def dht-flags\n  \"The flags this composition parses.  The engine's driver hands each of\n   them to `parse-flag` and never reads one itself.\"\n  #{\"--dht-peer\" \"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-bind\" \"--dht-port\"\n    \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes\" \"--dht-manifest\" \"--dht-key\" \"--dht-principal\"\n    \"--dht-trust\" \"--dht-follow\"})\n\n\n(def max-follow\n  \"The most principals one node follows (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 7).\"\n  64)\n\n\n(defn parse-follow\n  \"A `--dht-follow` value, `<64 hex>@<host:port>`, as `{:principal hex\n   :host h :port p}`: the principal whose published head is followed, at\n   the one address its board is dialed at.  The host must be a loopback\n   IP literal (`localhost` is 127.0.0.1): following off loopback is\n   not in this release (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.1, 8.3).\"\n  [text]\n  (let [[_ principal v6 v4 port]\n        (re-matches #\"(?:ed25519:)?([0-9a-f]{64})@(?:\\[([^\\]]+)\\]|([^:\\[\\]@]+)):(\\d+)\"\n                    (str/replace-first (str text) #\"@localhost:\" \"@127.0.0.1:\"))\n        host (or v6 v4)\n        port (repl.main/parse-int port)]\n    (cond\n      (nil? principal)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-follow takes <64 lowercase hex>@<host:port>,\"\n                           \" not \" (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      (not (datagram/valid-port? port))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-follow takes a port from 1 to 65535, not \"\n                           (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      (not (remote-channel/loopback-literal? host))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-follow \" (pr-str text) \": a head board is \"\n                           \"followed on loopback only (127.0.0.1 or ::1)\")\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      :else {:principal principal :host host :port port})))\n\n\n(defn parse-principal\n  \"A `--dht-principal` value: a declared publisher's public key, exactly\n   64 lowercase hexadecimal characters (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.2).\"\n  [text]\n  (if (and (string? text) (re-matches #\"^[0-9a-f]{64}$\" text))\n    text\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-principal takes a public key of 64 lowercase \"\n                         \"hexadecimal characters, not \" (pr-str text))\n                    {:value text}))))\n\n\n(defn parse-trust\n  \"Parse the shared CLI/session trust configuration principal.\"\n  [text]\n  (state/parse-trust text))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The publisher's key file (yin.vm.linker.dht.md 6.5)\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn split-path\n  \"`[dir name]` of a file path.\"\n  [path]\n  (if-let [i (str/last-index-of path \"/\")]\n    [(subs path 0 i) (subs path (inc i))]\n    [\".\" path]))\n\n\n(defn load-key\n  \"The publisher key `{:seed :public}` the key file at `path` holds, or a\n   refusal of startup with the reason: a file that does not exist, or one\n   `yin.vm.linker.sign/key-from-text` refuses.  Nothing falls back to a\n   fresh key, and no refusal carries the file's content.\"\n  [path]\n  (let [[dir name] (split-path path)\n        text (fs/read-file-text dir name)\n        key (when text (sign/key-from-text text))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? text)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-key \" path \": the key file does not exist; \"\n                           \"nothing falls back to a fresh key (create one with \"\n                           \"--dht-keygen \" path \")\")\n                      {:path path}))\n\n      (= :refused (:status key))\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-key \" path \": the key file is refused (\"\n                           (:reason key) \")\")\n                      {:path path :reason (:reason key)}))\n\n      :else key)))\n\n(defn- dht-spec\n  \"Fold the `--dht-*` flags into the `dht:<dir>` spec, checked by\n   `yin.shell.dht/checked-spec`.  They mean nothing to any other store,\n   and a bind address means nothing to a solo node, so each such use is\n   refused rather than ignored.\"\n  [spec {:keys [flags peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n                manifest follow principals]}]\n  (cond\n    (and (seq flags) (not= :dht (:type spec)))\n    (throw (ex-info (str (str/join \", \" (sort flags))\n                         \" need --index-store dht:<dir>\")\n                    {:flags (vec (sort flags))}))\n\n    (not= :dht (:type spec)) spec\n\n    (and (empty? peers) (or bind-host bind-port))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-bind and --dht-port need a --dht-peer: \"\n                         \"with no peers the DHT store is solo and opens \"\n                         \"no socket\")\n                    {}))\n\n    (and bind-host (not (datagram/ip-literal? bind-host)))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-bind must be an IP literal, not \"\n                         (pr-str bind-host))\n                    {:value bind-host}))\n\n    (and (seq follow) (empty? peers))\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-follow needs a --dht-peer: a followed head's \"\n                         \"index is fetched over the DHT\")\n                    {}))\n\n    (some #(not (contains? (set principals) (:principal %))) follow)\n    (let [p (:principal (first (remove #(contains? (set principals)\n                                                   (:principal %))\n                                       follow)))]\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"--dht-follow \" p \" follows a principal that is not\"\n                           \" declared: add --dht-principal \" p)\n                      {:principal p})))\n\n    (not= (count follow) (count (distinct (map :principal follow))))\n    (throw (ex-info \"--dht-follow names each principal once: one source each\"\n                    {}))\n\n    (> (count follow) max-follow)\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"at most \" max-follow \" principals may be followed\")\n                    {:count (count follow)}))\n\n    :else\n    (shell.dht/checked-spec\n      (cond-> (assoc spec :peers (vec peers) :publish? (boolean publish?))\n        bind-host (assoc :bind-host bind-host)\n        bind-port (assoc :bind-port bind-port)\n        max-inbound-bytes (assoc :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes)\n        manifest (assoc :manifest manifest)\n        ;; a pin wins for the run: it follows nothing (5.6)\n        (and (seq follow) (not manifest)) (assoc :follow (vec follow))\n        (and (seq follow) manifest) (assoc :follow-suspended true)))))\n\n\n(defn- dht-number\n  [flag text]\n  (or (repl.main/parse-int text)\n      (throw (ex-info (str flag \" takes an integer of at most 15 digits, not \"\n                           (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text}))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The subcommands: `keygen` and `dht init|serve|join`\n;; =============================================================================\n(defn- peer-text\n  \"A peer as the DHT takes it: `localhost` is the loopback IP literal.\"\n  [text]\n  (str/replace-first (str text) #\"^localhost:\" \"127.0.0.1:\"))\n\n\n(defn parse-token\n  \"A join token `yin:<host:port>/<principal>` as `[peer principal]` flag\n   values; the principal accepts an `ed25519:` prefix.  A token with a\n   third part is refused: a manifest is a pin and belongs to\n   `--dht-manifest` (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.8).\"\n  [text]\n  (let [[_ peer principal more]\n        (re-matches #\"yin:([^/]+)/(?:ed25519:)?([^/]+)(/.*)?\" (str text))]\n    (cond\n      (and peer more)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"a join token has two parts, yin:<host:port>/\"\n                           \"<principal>; \" (pr-str text) \" has a third: a \"\n                           \"manifest is a pin and belongs to --dht-manifest\")\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      (not peer)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"a join token looks like yin:<host:port>/\"\n                           \"<principal>, as `dht: join token:` prints it, \"\n                           \"not \" (pr-str text))\n                      {:value text}))\n\n      :else [peer principal])))\n\n\n(defn- keygen-args\n  [args]\n  (loop [args (seq args) name nil file nil]\n    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n      (if (= \"--name\" arg)\n        (recur (nnext args) (second args) file)\n        (recur (next args) name arg))\n      [\"--dht-keygen\" (or file (state-path (or name \"publisher\") \".key\"))])))\n\n\n(declare flag-table)\n\n\n(defn- global-flag-kind\n  [arg]\n  (or (get (:kinds flag-table) arg)\n      (when (contains? (:one-shot-flags flag-table) arg) :value)\n      (get {\"--name\" :value \"--dir\" :value\n            \"--reset\" :switch \"--no-state\" :switch} arg)))\n\n\n(defn- dht-args\n  \"The legacy flags of `dht init|serve|join`.  `init` publishes (its key is\n   made on first use); `serve` stores for others; `join <token>` reads,\n   declaring and following the token's principal at its address.\n   Every node needs a `--peer` to open a socket (the two-node start in\n   yin.repl.md); `--listen [ip:]port` is the node's own address.  Returns\n   `[args {:new-key path}]`.\"\n  [[verb & args]]\n  (when-not (#{\"init\" \"serve\" \"join\"} verb)\n    (throw (ex-info \"usage: yin-repl dht init|serve|join [token] [options]\"\n                    {})))\n  (loop [args (seq args)\n         o {:name \"node\" :peers [] :rest []}]\n    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n      (let [v (second args)]\n        (case arg\n          \"--name\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :name v))\n          \"--dir\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :dir v))\n          \"--key\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :key v))\n          \"--peer\" (recur (nnext args) (update o :peers conj (peer-text v)))\n          \"--listen\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :listen v))\n          (let [kind (global-flag-kind arg)]\n            (cond\n              (and kind (not= :switch kind))\n              (recur (nnext args) (update o :rest into [arg v]))\n\n              (and (= \"join\" verb) (not (:token o))\n                   (not (str/starts-with? arg \"-\")))\n              (recur (next args) (assoc o :token arg))\n\n              :else (recur (next args) (update o :rest conj arg))))))\n      (let [{:keys [name dir key peers listen token rest]} o\n            [tpeer principal] (when (= \"join\" verb)\n                                (parse-token token))\n            tpeer (some-> tpeer peer-text)\n            peers (cond-> peers tpeer (conj tpeer))\n            [_ lhost lport] (when listen\n                              (re-matches #\"(?:(.+):)?(\\d+)\" listen))\n            key (or key (when (= \"init\" verb) (state-path name \".key\")))]\n        [(cond-> [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (or dir (state-path name \"\")))]\n           (= \"init\" verb) (conj \"--dht-publish\")\n           key (into [\"--dht-key\" key])\n           lhost (into [\"--dht-bind\" lhost])\n           lport (into [\"--dht-port\" lport])\n           ;; join follows the principal's head at the token's address and\n           ;; passes no manifest: its first manifest is the first head it\n           ;; installs (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.8)\n           principal (into [\"--dht-principal\" principal\n                            \"--dht-follow\" (str principal \"@\" tpeer)])\n           true (into (mapcat #(vector \"--dht-peer\" %)) peers)\n           true (into rest))\n         {:new-key (when (= \"init\" verb) key)\n          :name name\n          :dir (or dir (state-path name \"\"))\n          ;; only `init` publishes and signs by default: a saved --dht-publish\n          ;; or --dht-key must not survive `serve` or `join` (explicit flags\n          ;; named on that command line still stand)\n          :unset (when-not (= \"init\" verb) #{\"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\"})}]))))\n\n\n(defn expand-args\n(defn parse-flag\n  \"The engine driver's `:flag-parser` hook: parse one flag this composition\n   owns out of `args`, answering `{:opts opts' :extra extra' :advance n}`,\n   `n` the arguments consumed including the flag itself — or nil for a flag\n   this composition does not own, which the driver then reads itself.\n\n   `extra` is the driver's opaque parse accumulator, handed back on every\n   answer: this composition gathers the flags it reads into it, and\n   `finalize-opts` folds them into the resolved `:index-store-spec` once\n   every argument has been read.  Two option keys cross into the driver's\n   own map, both neutral and both read back by it: `:publisher-key-file`,\n   the key file `--dht-key` named, and `:keygen`, the file `--dht-keygen`\n   named, which composes nothing and ends the run.\"\n  [arg value args opts extra]\n  (let [extra (cond-> extra (dht-flags arg) (update :flags conj arg))]\n    (case arg\n      \"--dht-peer\" {:extra (update extra :peers conj (parse-peer value))\n                    :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-publish\" {:extra (assoc extra :publish? true) :advance 1}\n      \"--dht-bind\" {:extra (assoc extra :bind-host (str value)) :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-port\" {:extra (assoc extra :bind-port (dht-number arg value))\n                    :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-max-inbound-bytes\"\n      {:extra (assoc extra :max-inbound-bytes (dht-number arg value))\n       :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-manifest\" {:extra (assoc extra :manifest (parse-manifest value))\n                        :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-key\"\n      {:opts (assoc opts :publisher-key-file\n                    (or value\n                        (throw (ex-info \"--dht-key needs a key file\" {})))\n                    :dht-key-file\n                    (or value\n                        (throw (ex-info \"--dht-key needs a key file\" {}))))\n       :extra extra\n       :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-principal\"\n      {:opts (update opts :principals (fnil conj []) (parse-principal value))\n       :extra extra\n       :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-trust\"\n      {:opts (update-in opts [:admission :trusted] (fnil conj #{})\n                        (parse-trust value))\n       :extra extra\n       :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-follow\" {:extra (update extra :follow (fnil conj [])\n                                     (parse-follow value))\n                      :advance 2}\n      \"--dht-keygen\"\n      {:opts (assoc opts :keygen\n                    (or value\n                        (throw (ex-info \"--dht-keygen needs a file\" {}))))\n       :extra extra\n       :advance 2}\n      nil)))\n\n\n(defn finalize-opts\n  \"The engine driver's `:finalize` hook: fold the flags the parse gathered\n   into `extra` into the resolved `:index-store-spec`.  A composition's\n   flags mean nothing to a store it does not name, so `dht-spec` refuses\n   rather than ignores them.\"\n  [opts extra]\n  (update opts :index-store-spec dht-spec\n          (assoc extra :principals (:principals opts))))\n\n\n(defn parse-store-arg\n  \"The `--index-store` value as a spec, over the engine's two schemes and\n   this composition's `dht:` (yin.shell.store/parse-arg).\"\n  [value]\n  (shell.store/parse-arg value))\n\n\n(def state-table\n  \"The saved-flag table this composition adds to the engine's own: every\n(defn ensure-key!\n  \"Write a new key file at `path` when nothing is there yet, answering the\n   lines to print, or nil when the file already exists.  This is what a\n   subcommand's `:new-key` asks for: `dht init` makes its key on first use\n   and reuses it afterwards, so a restart is still the same principal.\"\n  [path]\n  (let [[dir name] (split-path path)]\n    (when (nil? (fs/read-file-text dir name))\n      (:lines (keygen! path)))))\n\n\n(defn banner-lines\n  \"What the composition states before the first prompt, given parsed\n   options.  A DHT store states here — before its node steps once, so\n   before anything is shared — what it will share: the whole store when\n   `--dht-publish` is given, nothing otherwise (yin.shell.dht/banner).  The\n   publisher's own principal is read off the loaded `:publisher-key`, so\n   this namespace and not the engine's driver is the one that knows a key\n   has a principal.\"\n  [opts]\n  (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n        dht? (= :dht (:type spec))\n        publisher (some-> (:publisher-key opts) :public sign/principal)]\n    (if-not dht?\n      []\n      (cond-> (vec (shell.dht/banner spec))\n        (:publish? spec)\n        (conj (str \"dht: the code index and the code itself are shared: every\"\n                   \" evaluated program's rows are written to the index store\"\n                   \" each round\"))\n        publisher\n        (conj (str \"dht: names published here are signed by principal \"\n                   publisher \" (key from \" (:publisher-key-file opts) \")\"))\n        (not publisher)\n        (conj (str \"dht: no --dht-key: (yin.link/publish ...) is refused; names\"\n                   \" are still read, resolved, loaded and linked\"))))))\n\n\n(def keygen-flag\n  \"The one argument that composes nothing at all: the engine driver reads\n   no state file for such a run, and hands the path it named to `keygen!`.\"\n  \"--dht-keygen\")\n\n\n(defn hooks\n  \"The command-line half of the plain-data bundle `yin.repl.main` takes as\n   its `:composition`: every way this composition widens the engine\n   driver's argument surface, and nothing else.  The store, the session and\n   the transport lifecycle keys beside these are the outer host entry\n   point's to add (`yin.shell.main/composition`), so this namespace stays a\n   parser and never opens a socket.\"\n  []\n  {:flag-table flag-table\n   :expand-args expand-args\n   :flag-parser parse-flag\n   :parse-store-arg parse-store-arg\n   :initial-extra {:flags #{} :peers []}\n   :finalize finalize-opts\n   :keygen-flag keygen-flag\n   :keygen! keygen!\n   :ensure-key! ensure-key!\n   :load-key load-key\n   :banner-lines banner-lines\n   :help-lines help-lines})\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '540,740p;1282,1351p' src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc; rg -n 'bind-step|defn.*traffic' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc; sed -n '630,651p' docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '540,740p;1282,1351p' src/cljc/yin/shell/dht.cljc; rg -n 'bind-step|defn.*traffic' src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc; sed -n '630,651p' docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- compose\n  \"The two values `open` answers, over the joined `node`: `[handle node]`,\n   the generic `dao.jing` content handle the engine is handed and the\n   transport step-owner value this composition keeps.  The publisher's\n   board, the follower restored from `records`, a pinned hydration and the\n   HEAD write that announces and deposits are all on the node's side of\n   that split; only the handle, the recovery it read back and the\n   publication policy cross inward\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  [node base {:keys [dir manifest] :as checked} follow records\n   {:keys [key ws write-heads!]}]\n  (let [pub (publisher checked key base)\n        [follower node] (follower-of node dir follow records)\n        node (cond-> (assoc node ::dir dir ::ws ws)\n               pub (assoc ::publisher pub)\n               follower (assoc ::follower follower\n                               ::follow\n                               {:sources (into {}\n                                               (map (fn [f]\n                                                      [(sign/principal\n                                                         (:principal f))\n                                                       f]))\n                                               follow)\n                                :links {}\n                                :waiting {}\n                                :write! (or write-heads! fs/atomic-replace!)})\n               (and manifest (not= manifest (get-in base [:recovery\n                                                          :manifest])))\n               (-> (dht/load-index manifest)\n                   (assoc ::hydrating manifest)))]\n    ;; a recovered HEAD's trace, so a reader's first contact needs no new\n    ;; round (5.4)\n    (when-some [recovered (and pub (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n      (deposit-head! pub recovered))\n    [(assoc (dht/store node)\n            ;; The generic publication policy this composition declares\n            ;; (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 5), read\n            ;; off the injected handle by the engine so nothing\n            ;; downstream hardcodes a transport's page size.  Both halves\n            ;; are the transport's own answer (`publication-policy`): the\n            ;; count cap is storage's default, never this composition's\n            ;; message-size override, and the byte ceiling is derived from\n            ;; the bound the node actually composes under.  The store's own\n            ;; full-message refusal stays the last resort, exactly as §5\n            ;; preserves it.\n            :publication-policy (publication-policy node)\n            :head-fn (fn [manifest-address]\n                       ((:head-fn base) manifest-address)\n                       (dht/announce! node manifest-address)\n                       (when pub (deposit-head! pub manifest-address)))\n            :recovery (:recovery base)\n            ;; the reset-retention policy stated explicitly, so the engine\n            ;; never derives it from this composition's directory\n            ;; (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 6)\n            :retain-on-reset? true)\n     node]))\n\n\n(defn- quietly!\n  \"Run the cleanup `f`, swallowing what it throws: a cleanup never\n   replaces the refusal that caused it.\"\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n\n\n(defn open\n  \"Open a `dht:<dir>` store from its spec (`checked-spec`): the durable\n   directory store, and the `dao.space.dht` node joined over it.\n\n   Answers the two values of section 3's ownership split, and never one\n   value carrying both:\n\n   ```clojure\n   {:index-store <the generic dao.jing handle the engine is constructed\n                  with, carrying :head-fn, :recovery, :publication-policy\n                  and :retain-on-reset?>\n    :node <this composition's transport step-owner value>\n    :recovery <what the open validated, {:manifest :datoms}>\n    :publication-policy <the immutable generic policy of section 5>\n    :retain-index-on-reset? true}\n   ```\n\n   `opts`: `:key`, the publisher key `{:seed :public}`, which makes a\n   publishing node deposit its head; `:ws`, the host WebSocket seam\n   `{:connect! :bind! :unbind!}` (yin.repl.host) the board is served and\n   dialed over; `:write-heads!`, `(fn [dir name text])`, the atomic file\n   replace `heads.edn` is written with (`dao.space.store.fs` by\n   default); `:open-store`, `(fn [dir])`, the durable directory open\n   (`dao.space.store/open` by default).\n\n   A refusal releases everything it opened, exactly once, and is\n   answered as itself whatever the release throws: before the join the\n   directory store is closed; once joined the node owns it, and closing\n   the node closes the socket and then the store.\"\n  ([spec] (open spec {}))\n  ([spec {:keys [key ws write-heads! open-store]}]\n   (let [{:keys [dir peers publish? bind-host bind-port max-inbound-bytes\n                 manifest bind!]\n          :as checked} (checked-spec spec)\n         follow (checked-follow checked)\n         base ((or open-store durable/open) dir)\n         [node records]\n         (try\n           (when-some [why (refused-head dir manifest\n                                         (get-in base [:recovery :manifest]))]\n             (throw (ex-info why {:dir dir :manifest manifest})))\n           (let [records (heads-records dir follow)]\n             [(dht/join {:local base\n                         :peers peers\n                         :publish? publish?\n                         :bind-host bind-host\n                         :bind-port bind-port\n                         :max-inbound-bytes max-inbound-bytes\n                         :repair-slots default-repair-slots\n                         :bind! (or bind! (dht/default-bind))})\n              records])\n           (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n             (quietly! #(durable/close! base))\n             (throw e)))]\n     ;; from here the node owns the store and holds a socket\n     (try\n       (let [[index-store node]\n             (compose node base checked follow records\n                      {:key key :ws ws :write-heads! write-heads!})]\n         {:index-store index-store\n          :node node\n          :recovery (:recovery index-store)\n          :publication-policy (:publication-policy index-store)\n          :retain-index-on-reset? true})\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (quietly! #(dht/close! node))\n         (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn follower\n  \"The head follower a composition's `node` carries, or nil when it\n   follows nothing.\"\n  [node]\n  (get node ::follower))\n\n\n(defn stop!\n  \"Initiate the head composition's exit on `session`'s node: the board's\n   server is asked to stop (`head.board/stop!`), every follow dial is\n   closed and no dial is composed again, and the node is marked\n   stopping.  Performs no other I/O; `step` completes the stop and\n   `stopped?` reports it.  A session without a node, or one already\n   stopping, is answered unchanged.  The board serves a read-only ring\n   that stop does not end, so a reader has nothing to be told but the\n   reattachable close its connection observes.\n\n   This composition is the one resource owner: a host asks once, here,\n   and never closes a board, a dial or the store itself\n   (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md sections 3 and 6).\"\n  [session]\n  (let [node (:node session)]\n    (if (or (nil? node) (::stopping? node))\n      session\n      (do (doseq [[_ {:keys [dial]}] (get-in node [::follow :links])]\n            (when dial (head.board/close! dial)))\n          (assoc session :node\n                 (cond-> (assoc node ::stopping? true)\n                   (get-in node [::publisher :server])\n                   (update-in [::publisher :server] head.board/stop!)\n\n                   (::follow node)\n                   (assoc-in [::follow :links] {})))))))\n\n\n(defn stopped?\n  \"True when the head composition owes nothing at exit: no node, no\n   board server, or a board server that is stopped or refused.\"\n  [session]\n  (let [server (get-in session [:node ::publisher :server])]\n    (or (nil? server) (head.board/stopped? server))))\n\n\n(defn close!\n  \"The last resort after the exit drain's budget\n   (`yin.repl.main/stop-ticks`): whatever the board still owes is asked\n   for once more and not awaited.  The ordinary exit is `stop!`, then\n   `step` until `stopped?`.  A session never stopped is stopped first, so\n   a direct caller (a test, an embedder without a drain) still closes the\n   dials; the board's stopping tick runs at the node's last tick reading\n   only when the board is not already `stopped?`.\n\n   The store's own resources are the durable handle's `:close-fn`, which\n   the composition's single resource owner releases after this\n   (`yin.shell.main/close-composition!`), so nothing here is closed\n   twice.\"\n  [session]\n  (let [session (stop! session)\n        node (:node session)\n        server (get-in node [::publisher :server])]\n    (when (and server (not (head.board/stopped? server)))\n      (head.board/serve-step server (or (::now node) 0)))\n    nil))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n(defn step\n  \"Advance the composition's node once at the host's clock reading `now`\n   (dao.space.dht/step) and answer `[session' lines events]`: its events\n   as lines, and as the data the ticker reads to re-check a pending\n   require, a completed hydration installed, a failed one or a failed\n   bind recorded as the session's refusal.  The head composition steps\n   after the node: the board's endpoint (and the join token once it is\n   bound), then the follower, whose events join the node's.  A session\n   without a transport is answered unchanged.\n\n   `events` stay in this composition's own vocabulary: the host translates\n   them before anything crosses inward\n   (`yin.shell.completion/completion-events`), so the engine re-checks\n   only correlated generic completions and never decodes a transport\n   keyword (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md section 7).\"\n  [session now]\n  (if-let\n    [node (:node session)]\n    (let\n      [[node events] (dht/step node now)\n       node (assoc node ::now now)\n       node (reduce (fn [node {:keys [host port], :as event}]\n                      (cond-> node\n                        (= :bound (::dht/event event))\n                        (assoc ::listen [host port])))\n                    node\n                    events)\n       lines (mapv #(event-line node %) events)\n       [node board-lines] (if-some [pub (::publisher node)]\n                            (let [[pub ls] (step-board pub node events now)]\n                              [(assoc node ::publisher pub) ls])\n                            [node []])\n       [node follow-lines head-events] (step-follow session node now)\n       lines (-> lines (into board-lines) (into follow-lines))\n       hydrating (::hydrating node)\n       status (when hydrating (:status (dht/load-status node hydrating)))\n       node (cond->\n              node\n              (and hydrating (= :failed status))\n              (assoc\n                ::refusal (str/join\n                            \"\\n\" (filter\n                                   #(str/includes?\n                                      %\n                                      \"refused\")\n                                   lines)))\n              (dht/refusal node)\n              (assoc ::refusal (dht/refusal node)))\n       session (assoc session :node node)]\n      [(if (= :loaded status) (hydrated session node) session)\n       lines\n       (into (vec events) head-events)])\n    [session [] []]))\n\n\n(defn refusal\n  \"The text that refused the composition's store after startup (a failed\n   bind or a hydration that could not complete), or nil.\n\n   `session` is the composition session this namespace's every function\n   takes — `{:engine … :node … :key …}`, `yin.shell.session/make`'s shape —\n   and the node is read off its `:node` key and nowhere else: one contract\n   for `step`, `stop!`, `stopped?`, `close!`, `busy?`, `follow-lines`,\n   `refusal` and `admitting?`, so a host cannot step one of them into\n   silence by storing the node under a name only another of them reads.\"\n  [session]\n  (get (:node session) ::refusal))\n\n\n(defn admitting?\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:459:(defn- bind-step\nsrc/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc:1435:          [node bound] (bind-step node)\nsrc/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc:980:(defn- on-traffic\nresults cannot settle it; rollback does not replay a settled service\nrequest. A fresh engine-only JVM test process is started and the test\nasserts that the DHT namespaces were not loaded.\n\nThe whole retained engine suite, including this subset, is required on\nJVM, Node, and Dart, with guarded bodies enabled (`DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1`\nwhere applicable). Actual executed tests are recorded, not only\nnamespace loading.\n\nDHT-specific tests move with composition. They are not deleted and are\nnot counted as the non-DHT proof. The boundary merge still requires their\nexisting assertions — including eight distinct acknowledged publications,\nthe twenty-round/400-tick idle fixture, head-follow persistence,\nbind/hydration refusal, and shutdown — to pass on the affected host\nmatrix. One correction from the charter applies to that set: the \"eight\ndistinct\" assertion at `test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc:2097` counts manifest\naddresses, not acknowledgement timestamps. A failure there is diagnosed\nas failed publication or HEAD advancement, not relaxed as a supposed\ntiming pin.\n\n## 11. Nightly exposure during the refactor window\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
